{
  "title": "85: al-Burooj البروج",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nوَالسَّمَآءِ ذَاتِ الْبُرُوْجِۙ‏(1)\nWAS SAMAAA-E ZAATIL BOROOJE.\nBy the sky, (displaying) the Zodiacal Signs; \nوَالْيَوْمِ الْمَوْعُوْدِۙ‏(2)\nWAL YAWMIL MAW-O’ODE.\nBy the promised Day (of Judgment); \nوَشَاهِدٍ وَّمَشْهُوْدٍؕ‏(3)\nWA SHAAHEDINW WA MASHHOOD.\nBy one that witnesses, and the subject of the witness;- \nقُتِلَ اَصْحٰبُ الْاُخْدُوْدِۙ‏(4)\nQOTELA ASHAABUL UKHDOODIN.\nWoe to the makers of the pit (of fire), \nالنَّارِ ذَاتِ الْوَقُوْدِۙ‏(5)\nNAARE ZAATIL WAQOODE.\nFire supplied (abundantly) with fuel: \nاِذْ هُمْ عَلَيْهَا قُعُوْدٌ ۙ‏(6)\nIZ HUM A’LAYHAA QO-O’ODUNW.\nBehold! they sat over against the (fire), \nوَّهُمْ عَلٰى مَا يَفْعَلُوْنَ بِالْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ شُهُوْدٌ ؕ‏(7)\nWA HUM A’LAA MAA YAF-A’LOONA BIL-MOA-MENEENA SHO-HOOD.\nAnd they witnessed (all) that they were doing against the Believers. \nوَمَا نَقَمُوْا مِنْهُمْ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يُّؤْمِنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ الْعَزِيْزِ الْحَمِيْدِۙ‏(8)\nWA MAA NAQAMOO MINHUM ILLAA AN-Y YOA-MENOO BIL-LAAHIL A’ZEEZIL HAMEEDIL.\nAnd they ill-treated them for no other reason than that they believed in Allah, Exalted in Power, Worthy of all Praise!- \nالَّذِىْ لَهٗ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ؕ وَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ شَهِيْدٌ ؕ‏(9)\nLAZEE LAHOO MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL-ARZ, WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN SHAHEED.\nHim to Whom belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth! And Allah is Witness to all things. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ فَتَنُوا الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَ الْمُؤْمِنٰتِ ثُمَّ لَمْ يَتُوْبُوْا فَلَهُمْ عَذَابُ جَهَنَّمَ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابُ الْحَرِيْقِؕ‏(10)\nINNAL LAZEENA FATANUL MOA-MENEENA WAL MOAMENAATE SUMMA LAM YATOOBOO FALAHUM A’ZAABO JAHANNAMA WA LAHUM A’ZAABUL HAREEQ.\nThose who persecute (or draw into temptation) the Believers, men and women, and do not turn in repentance, will have the Penalty of Hell: They will have the Penalty of the Burning Fire. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ لَهُمْ جَنّٰتٌ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ ؕؔ ذٰلِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْكَبِيْرُؕ‏(11)\nINNAL LAAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE LAHUM JANNAATUN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAAR, ZAALEKAL FAWZUL KABEER.\nFor those who believe and do righteous deeds, will be Gardens; beneath which rivers flow: That is the great Salvation, (the fulfilment of all desires), \nاِنَّ بَطْشَ رَبِّكَ لَشَدِيْدٌ ؕ‏(12)\nINNA BATSHA RABBEKA LA-SHADEED.\nTruly strong is the Grip (and Power) of thy Lord. \nاِنَّهٗ هُوَ يُبْدِئُ وَيُعِيْدُ‌ ۚ‏(13)\nINNAHU HOWA YUBDEO WA YO-E’ED.\nIt is He Who creates from the very beginning, and He can restore (life). \nوَهُوَ الْغَفُوْرُ الْوَدُوْدُۙ‏(14)\nWA HOWAL GHAFOORUL WADOODO.\nAnd He is the Oft-Forgiving, Full of Loving-Kindness, \nذُو الْعَرْشِ الْمَجِيْدُ ۙ‏(15)\nZUL A’RSHIL MAJEEDO.\nLord of the Throne of Glory, \nفَعَّالٌ لِّمَا يُرِيْدُ ؕ‏(16)\nFA’-A’ALUL LEMAA YOREED.\nDoer (without let) of all that He intends. \nهَلْ اَتٰٮكَ حَدِيْثُ الْجُنُوْدِۙ‏(17)\nHAL ATAAKA HADEESUL JONOODE.\nHas the story reached thee, of the forces- \nفِرْعَوْنَ وَثَمُوْدَؕ‏(18)\nFIR-A’WNA WA SAMOOD.\nOf Pharaoh and the Thamud? \nبَلِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا فِىْ تَكْذِيْبٍۙ‏(19)\nBALIL LAZEENA KAFAROO FEE TAKZEEBINW.\nAnd yet the Unbelievers (persist) in rejecting (the Truth)! \nوَّاللّٰهُ مِنْ وَّرَآئِهِمْ مُّحِيْطٌۚ‏(20)\nWAL LAAHO MINW WA-RAAA-EHIM MOHEET.\nBut Allah doth encompass them from behind! \nبَلْ هُوَ قُرْاٰنٌ مَّجِيْدٌ ۙ‏(21)\nBAL HOWA QURAANUM MAJEEDUN.\nNay, this is a Glorious Qur'an, \nفِىْ لَوْحٍ مَّحْفُوْظٍ‏(22)\nFEE LAWHIM MAHFOOZ.\n(Inscribed) in a Tablet Preserved! ",
  "merits": "Surah al-Burooj (The Mansion Of Stars)\nThis ‘Makki’ Surah has 22 verses. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the one who recites this Surah will be near the Prophets and Messengers on the Day of Judgement. The reward for reciting this Surah is ten times the number of people who gather on the plains of Arafah.\nReciting this Surah saves one from dangers and if recited before sleeping, one is kept under the protection of Allah (s.w.t.) for the whole night. When trying to wean a baby (stop it from breastfeeding and start eating solid foods), this Surah should be written and tied as a talisman around the baby’s neck."
